HST Office: closing the last document over UNO no longer crashes the office on macOS (headless).

The application's main menu (SalNSMainMenu, made in initAppMenu) was autoreleased, so NSApp held the only
reference. Every menubar AquaSalMenu points at it without a reference of its own, and unsetMainMenu() calls
[NSApp setMainMenu:nil] before it removes the items. In headless mode nothing else (no drawn menu bar) holds the
menu, so restoring the default menu when the last document's menubar went away (setDefaultMenu, run on the main
thread for the UNO thread) sent numberOfItems to a deallocated SalNSMainMenu: Signal 11, NSZombieEnabled reports
"-[SalNSMainMenu numberOfItems]: message sent to deallocated instance". The main menu is now kept for the life
of the application.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/runtime/check-close-last-doc.py (macOS save replace probe workflow)
---
--- a/vcl/osx/salmenu.cxx
+++ b/vcl/osx/salmenu.cxx
@@ -130,7 +130,12 @@
 
     // Related: tdf#126638 use NSMenu subclass to catch and redirect key
     // shortcuts when a modal window is displayed
-    SalNSMainMenu* pMainMenu = [[[SalNSMainMenu alloc] initWithTitle: @"Main Menu"] autorelease];
+    // HST Office: the main menu is kept (not autoreleased) for the life of the application. Every
+    // menubar uses it ([NSApp mainMenu] in the AquaSalMenu constructor) without a reference of its
+    // own, and unsetMainMenu() sets the application's main menu to nil before it removes the items:
+    // when nothing else holds the menu (headless mode, where the menu bar is never drawn), that
+    // deallocated it, and closing the last document over UNO crashed in setDefaultMenu().
+    SalNSMainMenu* pMainMenu = [[SalNSMainMenu alloc] initWithTitle: @"Main Menu"];
     pNewItem = [pMainMenu addItemWithTitle: @"Application"
         action: nil
         keyEquivalent: @""];
